{"audio": "matthew-06.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 252800, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 1067, "text": "Matthew, Chapter Six."}, {"start_ms": 1067, "end_ms": 8267, "text": "Take heed that ye do not your alms before men, to be seen of them: otherwise ye have no reward of your Father which is in heaven."}, {"start_ms": 8267, "end_ms": 17067, "text": "Therefore when thou doest thine alms, do not sound a trumpet before thee, as the hypocrites do in the synagogues and in the streets, that they may have glory of men."}, {"start_ms": 17067, "end_ms": 19867, "text": "Verily I say unto you, They have their reward."}, {"start_ms": 19867, "end_ms": 32000, "text": "But when thou doest alms, let not thy left hand know what thy right hand doeth: That thine alms may be in secret: and thy Father which seeth in secret himself shall reward thee openly."}, {"start_ms": 32000, "end_ms": 41200, "text": "And when thou prayest, thou shalt not be as the hypocrites are: for they love to pray standing in the synagogues and in the corners of the streets, that they may be seen of men."}, {"start_ms": 41200, "end_ms": 45200, "text": "Verily I say unto you, They have their reward."}, {"start_ms": 45200, "end_ms": 56400, "text": "But thou, when thou prayest, enter into thy closet, and when thou hast shut thy door, pray to thy Father which is in secret; and thy Father which seeth in secret shall reward thee openly."}, {"start_ms": 56400, "end_ms": 64133, "text": "But when ye pray, use not vain repetitions, as the heathen do: for they think that they shall be heard for their much speaking."}, {"start_ms": 64133, "end_ms": 71067, "text": "Be not ye therefore like unto them: for your Father knoweth what things ye have need of, before ye ask him."}, {"start_ms": 71067, "end_ms": 77733, "text": "After this manner therefore pray ye: Our Father which art in heaven, Hallowed be thy name."}, {"start_ms": 77733, "end_ms": 79200, "text": "Thy kingdom come."}, {"start_ms": 79200, "end_ms": 82000, "text": "Thy will be done in earth, as it is in heaven."}, {"start_ms": 82000, "end_ms": 85200, "text": "Give us this day our daily bread."}, {"start_ms": 85200, "end_ms": 87733, "text": "And forgive us our debts, as we forgive our debtors."}, {"start_ms": 87733, "end_ms": 95733, "text": "And lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil: For thine is the kingdom, and the power, and the glory, for ever."}, {"start_ms": 95733, "end_ms": 96667, "text": "Amen."}, {"start_ms": 96667, "end_ms": 106933, "text": "For if ye forgive men their trespasses, your heavenly Father will also forgive you: But if ye forgive not men their trespasses, neither will your Father forgive your trespasses."}, {"start_ms": 106933, "end_ms": 115467, "text": "Moreover when ye fast, be not, as the hypocrites, of a sad countenance: for they disfigure their faces, that they may appear unto men to fast."}, {"start_ms": 115467, "end_ms": 118667, "text": "Verily I say unto you, They have their reward."}, {"start_ms": 118667, "end_ms": 131867, "text": "But thou, when thou fastest, anoint thine head, and wash thy face; That thou appear not unto men to fast, but unto thy Father which is in secret: and thy Father, which seeth in secret, shall reward thee openly."}, {"start_ms": 131867, "end_ms": 148800, "text": "Lay not up for yourselves treasures upon earth, where moth and rust doth corrupt, and where thieves break through and steal: But lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust doth corrupt, and where thieves do not break through nor steal: For where your treasure is,"}, {"start_ms": 148800, "end_ms": 150667, "text": "there will your heart be also."}, {"start_ms": 150667, "end_ms": 157067, "text": "The light of the body is the eye: if therefore thine eye be single, thy whole body shall be full of light."}, {"start_ms": 157067, "end_ms": 161067, "text": "But if thine eye be evil, thy whole body shall be full of darkness."}, {"start_ms": 161067, "end_ms": 165600, "text": "If therefore the light that is in thee be darkness, how great is that darkness!"}, {"start_ms": 165600, "end_ms": 174133, "text": "No man can serve two masters: for either he will hate the one, and love the other; or else he will hold to the one, and despise the other."}, {"start_ms": 174133, "end_ms": 176400, "text": "Ye cannot serve God and mammon."}, {"start_ms": 176400, "end_ms": 185600, "text": "Therefore I say unto you, Take no thought for your life, what ye shall eat, or what ye shall drink; nor yet for your body, what ye shall put on."}, {"start_ms": 185600, "end_ms": 188800, "text": "Is not the life more than meat, and the body than raiment?"}, {"start_ms": 188800, "end_ms": 197600, "text": "Behold the fowls of the air: for they sow not, neither do they reap, nor gather into barns; yet your heavenly Father feedeth them."}, {"start_ms": 197600, "end_ms": 199733, "text": "Are ye not much better than they?"}, {"start_ms": 199733, "end_ms": 203867, "text": "Which of you by taking thought can add one cubit unto his stature?"}, {"start_ms": 203867, "end_ms": 206533, "text": "And why take ye thought for raiment?"}, {"start_ms": 206533, "end_ms": 216933, "text": "Consider the lilies of the field, how they grow; they toil not, neither do they spin: And yet I say unto you, That even Solomon in all his glory was not arrayed like one of these."}, {"start_ms": 216933, "end_ms": 225333, "text": "Wherefore, if God so clothe the grass of the field, which to day is, and to morrow is cast into the oven, shall he not much more clothe you, O ye of little faith?"}, {"start_ms": 225333, "end_ms": 228267, "text": "Therefore take no thought, saying, What shall we eat?"}, {"start_ms": 228267, "end_ms": 229467, "text": "or, What shall we drink?"}, {"start_ms": 229467, "end_ms": 232133, "text": "or, Wherewithal shall we be clothed?"}, {"start_ms": 232133, "end_ms": 238533, "text": "(For after all these things do the Gentiles seek:) for your heavenly Father knoweth that ye have need of all these things."}, {"start_ms": 238533, "end_ms": 244933, "text": "But seek ye first the kingdom of God, and his righteousness; and all these things shall be added unto you."}, {"start_ms": 244933, "end_ms": 250000, "text": "Take therefore no thought for the morrow: for the morrow shall take thought for the things of itself."}, {"start_ms": 250000, "end_ms": 252800, "text": "Sufficient unto the day is the evil thereof."}], "words": [{"t": "Matthew,", "s": 81, "e": 342, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 362, "e": 664, "si": 0}, {"t": "Six.", "s": 725, "e": 946, "si": 0}, {"t": "Take", "s": 1248, "e": 1488, "si": 1}, {"t": "heed", "s": 1528, "e": 1809, "si": 1}, {"t": "that", "s": 1849, "e": 1990, "si": 1}, {"t": "ye", "s": 2050, "e": 2130, "si": 1}, {"t": "do", "s": 2230, "e": 2290, "si": 1}, {"t": "not", "s": 2391, "e": 2591, "si": 1}, {"t": "your", "s": 2631, "e": 2772, "si": 1}, {"t": "alms", "s": 2852, "e": 3093, "si": 1}, {"t": "before", "s": 3133, "e": 3514, "si": 1}, {"t": "men,", "s": 3554, "e": 3795, "si": 1}, {"t": "to", "s": 4256, "e": 4316, "si": 1}, {"t": "be", "s": 4356, "e": 4416, "si": 1}, {"t": "seen", "s": 4537, "e": 4757, "si": 1}, {"t": "of", "s": 4817, "e": 4878, "si": 1}, {"t": "them:", "s": 4918, "e": 5058, "si": 1}, {"t": "otherwise", "s": 5399, "e": 5840, "si": 1}, {"t": "ye", "s": 5860, "e": 5941, "si": 1}, {"t": "have", "s": 6001, "e": 6181, "si": 1}, {"t": "no", "s": 6221, "e": 6302, "si": 1}, {"t": "reward", "s": 6382, "e": 6823, "si": 1}, {"t": "of", "s": 6863, "e": 6923, "si": 1}, {"t": "your", "s": 6943, "e": 7064, "si": 1}, {"t": "Father", "s": 7124, "e": 7445, "si": 1}, {"t": "which", "s": 7485, "e": 7645, "si": 1}, {"t": "is", "s": 7685, "e": 7766, "si": 1}, {"t": "in", "s": 7826, "e": 7906, "si": 1}, {"t": "heaven.", "s": 7966, "e": 8227, "si": 1}, {"t": "Therefore", "s": 8708, "e": 9049, "si": 2}, {"t": "when", "s": 9049, "e": 9189, "si": 2}, {"t": "thou", "s": 9229, "e": 9370, "si": 2}, {"t": "doest", "s": 9450, "